MDI lines sent behind a remapped M400 that yields INTERP_EXECUTE_FINISH
wait for it and run in order.  Task sets its plan wait while the remap is
suspended, and an MDI arriving then is queued instead of being handed to
the interpreter, which would drop it (7e640f7b08).  The test checks the
order the lines and the remap report in, through the operator messages,
and that nothing crashed.  It cannot hit the one task cycle the wait flag
guards on its own: linuxcnc.command waits for task to take each line.
